		{
			"color": {
				"a": 1.0,
				"b": 0.300000011920929,
				"g": 0.25,
				"r": 0.200000002980232,
				"type": "Color"
			},
			"name": "About",
			"node_position": {
				"x": 0.0,
				"y": -320.0
			},
			"parameters": {},
			"seed": -320.0,
			"size": {
				"x": 900.0,
				"y": 200.0
			},
			"text": "Heritage copper roofing, weathered to a grey verdigris: the painted steel photograph tinted a dull patina green (Charcoal), in pans eight across a repeat with a shade of their own each (Pans, PanTone) and a shadow line at each seam (SeamLine, SeamMask, SeamShade); RibNormal raises the seams as ribs over the photograph's normal map. A patina, not bare metal: the Material's Metallic factor cuts the photograph's to near none. Lay it with the seams running down the slope.",
			"title": "Copper",
			"type": "comment"
		},
